# The llama.cpp release and the model the real-runtime test runs on and the image ships (INFER-llama
# G4, INFER-image G5).
# .github/workflows/infer-real.yml downloads each file, checks its SHA-256 against the value
# here and fails on a mismatch, so a changed upstream asset is never run. Key=value, no spaces.
# Changing a pin changes what the real test proves: read ASSUMPTIONS INFER-A13 first.
#
# llama.cpp release b11900 (2026-10-26), its source as GitHub serves the tag. image/llamaserver.sh
# builds llama-server from exactly this file, CPU only and static; infer-real runs the real test on
# that build and the image ships it (INFER-image, #3655). `unpinned` makes the workflow print the
# file's hash and fail, which is how the pin is taken (the hash of a file downloaded in CI, never a
# value typed from memory).
# The archive carries the commit it was made from; llama_src_commit pins it, and infer-real checks
# that the tag b11900 names that commit over git (git ls-remote), a path apart from the archive.
llama_src_url=https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/archive/refs/tags/b11900.tar.gz
llama_src_sha256=14785acc1ab3f9356df6329941a363a81217ba35e28ea7f95da36bbeee33dab9
llama_src_commit=74b104c9ba5717116b7e65e0cd35397778653304
# The model, Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B at Q8_0 (D-230), 639150592 bytes, at the Hugging Face revision
# below. Apache-2.0: its GGUF header's general.license, which the image build reads and checks
# (INFER-A4). The SHA-256 is the LFS object id Hugging Face publishes for the file, read from its
# API on 2026-10-28 and equal to the hash of the file downloaded then. The real test runs on the
# file the image installs.
embed_url=https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-GGUF/resolve/370f27d7550e0def9b39c1f16d3fbaa13aa67728/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf
embed_sha256=06507c7b42688469c4e7298b0a1e16deff06caf291cf0a5b278c308249c3e439
